# Tablebase-conversion suite positions — see test/tb_conversion.py.
#
# Every line is `<FEN> ; <material> dtz=<D> budget=<rule50+D>/100`, and every
# one is a position White WINS according to Syzygy AT THE STATED HALFMOVE
# CLOCK: Fathom's root probe reports TB_WIN, which by dtz_to_wdl()
# (src/syzygy/tbprobe.cpp:559) means `dtz + rule50 <= 100`. Generated and then
# re-verified at the stated clock with ./tools/tbdefend — a position that were
# only winnable at clock 0 would make the whole suite lie, since the suite's
# core assertion is that the win survives the 50-move counter.
#
# The first three are the endgame from the reported production game (KNP vs KB,
# a genuine win — Stockfish 18 gives mate in 18 from the fresh-clock version).
# Through the HTTP serve path the engine shuffled its knight for 28 plies at a
# flat +314.96 and drew it; through UCI, which is the only caller of
# TB::probe_root, it mated.
#
# Several lines carry a deliberately TIGHT budget (90+/100). That is the actual
# failure mode: with a fresh clock even an aimless engine stumbles into the win
# eventually, so a suite of clock-0 positions would pass on the broken code.
#
# Regenerate/verify:  ./tools/tbdefend < <(gawk -F' ;' '!/^#/&&NF{print $1}' test/tb_positions.epd)

8/6Pb/5K2/4N3/4k3/8/8/8 w - - 71 93 ; KNPvKB  (game position) dtz=15 budget=86/100
